From: =?UTF-8?q?=C3=98yvind=20Harboe?= <oyvind.harboe@zylin.com>
Subject: [PATCH] grt: store the 3D maze's parents in 16 bit coordinates
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

pr_3D_ holds the parent of every GCell and layer during 3D maze routing
as an int16 layer and two int coordinates, 12 bytes. Grid coordinates
are int16 everywhere else in FastRoute (TreeNode, the 2D parents), so
the parent fits in 6 bytes. On a 34 M GCell x 9 layer die that is about
1.8 GB less.

Carried in bazel-orfs for OpenROAD#12075, not upstreamed; retires with
the //:bump onto an OpenROAD that has it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Øyvind Harboe <oyvind.harboe@zylin.com>
---
 src/grt/src/fastroute/include/FastRoute.h | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/grt/src/fastroute/include/FastRoute.h b/src/grt/src/fastroute/include/FastRoute.h
index 0dc7d44770..b00ff743e5 100644
--- a/src/grt/src/fastroute/include/FastRoute.h
+++ b/src/grt/src/fastroute/include/FastRoute.h
@@ -75,7 +75,7 @@ struct DebugSetting
 struct parent3D
 {
   int16_t layer;
-  int x, y;
+  int16_t x, y;  // grid coordinates are int16_t, as in TreeNode
 };
 
 struct CostParams
